---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CALL_HREF } from "../../siteConfig";

const title = "Your brand shouldn't live in a PDF";
const description = "Brand guidelines nobody reads, and what to replace them with: a brief that AI tools can actually use.";
const date = "June 26, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} · Nrvana Studio`} description={description}>
  <section class="section pt-24 pb-6">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest" style="color: var(--color-accent-deep);">Plates · Brand</div>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[0.95] max-w-3xl">
      {title}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink-mute);">{date}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-10">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>You have brand guidelines. Maybe they're a careful, designed document (color palettes, font stacks, logo clearspace, the works). Maybe they're rougher: a shared folder, a Notion page, a loose collection of reference screenshots.</p>
      <p>Either way, nobody is reading them.</p>
      <p>Not regularly. Not your contractors. Certainly not the AI tools you're now trying to use to work faster.</p>
      <p>This isn't a critique of your guidelines. It's that the PDF format was designed for a different era. Here's what works instead.</p>

      <h2>Why PDF brand guides don't transfer</h2>
      <p>A style guide describes what your brand looks like. It doesn't tell a tool how to think, decide, or make trade-offs in your voice and aesthetic. It doesn't answer the questions that come up in real creative work: "Should this headline be punchy or understated?" "What image fits here when the template doesn't?" "Would we do this in red or let it breathe?"</p>
      <p>Those are judgment calls. Brand guides describe outcomes. They don't embed judgment.</p>
      <p>AI tools need something closer to a briefing than a rulebook.</p>

      <h2>What AI actually needs to sound and look like you</h2>
      <p>Three things.</p>
      <p><strong>A voice file.</strong> Not adjectives about your brand ("bold, warm, direct"). Examples. Two or three sentences written in your voice, next to the same idea written the way you'd never write it. The contrast is what a tool can actually learn from.</p>
      <p><strong>A visual direction note.</strong> Not hex codes and font sizes. Intent. "We're editorial, not corporate. Photography over illustration, white space over density, serif display type." The feeling, not the spec sheet.</p>
      <p><strong>A prompt library.</strong> Fifteen to twenty-five ready-to-use prompts tuned to your actual output types: deck slides, social captions, email headers, product mockups, copy variations. Templates that already know what you're going for, so you start from 80% instead of zero.</p>
      <p>Together, these are what we call a <strong>Visual Cortex</strong>. Your brand, in a form AI tools can read.</p>

      <h2>The 15-minute start</h2>
      <p>You don't need to rebuild your guidelines. Start smaller.</p>
      <p>Open a blank document and write three things:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>One paragraph about who your audience is and what they should feel after experiencing your brand at its best.</li>
        <li>Three sentences you'd be proud to have written (not aspirational: actual sentences that sound like you).</li>
        <li>Two things that are off-limits. ("Never use corporate stock photography." "Never use the word 'innovative.'")</li>
      </ol>
      <p>That's the nucleus. Everything else grows from there.</p>

      <h2>The full thing</h2>
      <p>We build out the complete Visual Cortex in our <a href="/services/snapshot">Design Snapshot</a> and <a href="/services/visual-cortex">Personal Visual Cortex</a> engagements. You leave with a brand that AI tools can actually use, which means faster output that consistently looks and sounds like you, not like a template.</p>
      <p><a href={CALL_HREF}>Book a free 30-minute call</a> if you'd like to talk through your situation first.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-16">
    <div class="rounded-2xl p-10 text-center" style="background-color: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-canvas);">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold">Give your brand a memory.</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/services/visual-cortex" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-6 py-3 font-medium"
           style="background-color: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-canvas);">
          See the Visual Cortex ($2,500)
        </a>
        <a href={CALL_HREF} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-6 py-3 underline underline-offset-4"
           style="color: var(--color-canvas-soft);">
          Book a free 30-minute call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-8">
    <a href="/plates" class="text-sm underline underline-offset-4" style="color: var(--color-ink-mute);">← All plates</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
